    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe rename/signature changes, doc updates, removal of the now-dead `inHousehold` helper, and the controller guard-clause additions are all clean and consistent with the surrounding code. Two structural points, though, stem from `assignHousehold` changing character \u2014 it went from a DB-mutating \"place owner into household + back-fill existing members\" operation to a pure, local derivation from the owner's own two fields:\n\n1. **`assignHousehold`/`generateHouseholdId` is now a pure derivation but still lives as a `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` service method** (`ClinicServiceImpl.java:338-344`). It no longer touches `ownerRepository` at all, so the `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` annotation is now misleading \u2014 it advertises DB work that doesn't happen. More importantly, `Owner.getIdentityKey()` (`Owner.java:213`) is already a derived value computed *on the model*, and the household id is now exactly the same kind of thing: a deterministic function of the owner's own fields. Deriving `householdId` on the `Owner` model (mirroring `getIdentityKey`) would put the logic in the more natural unit, and the `MessageDigest`/hex code would sit next to the key it feeds.\n\n2. **The derivation-as-side-effect creates temporal coupling the controller now has to manage by hand.** Because `getIdentityKey()` reads `householdId`, the controller must remember to call `this.clinicService.assignHousehold(owner)` *before* `isIdentityKeyInUse` / `isHouseholdInUse` or detection silently misbehaves \u2014 the comment at `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:142-145` (\"Assign it before the identity key is computed\") is documenting exactly this fragility. If `householdId` were derived lazily on the model like `identityKey`, this ordering requirement and the explicit `assignHousehold` orchestration step disappear entirely.\n\nConsider moving the household-id derivation onto `Owner` (next to `getIdentityKey`) so both derived keys live together and the controller no longer carries an ordering obligation; at minimum drop the now-inapplicable `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` from `assignHousehold`.",
